<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kost Levytsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1859–1941</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kostiantyn Levytsky</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kost Levytsky was a Ukrainian lawyer and politician in Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, a leader of the National <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-party-united-states">Democratic Party</a> and member of the Austrian parliament. In November 1918 he headed the first government of the West Ukrainian People's Republic, the State Secretariat, under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yevhen-petrushevych">Yevhen Petrushevych</a>. In 1941 he briefly chaired the Ukrainian National Council in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> before his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kost-levytsky.jpg" alt="Kost Levytsky" width="320" height="476" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown-anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Levytsky_Kost-1-.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
